{#
  The homepage audit, as a page. Built on the contact page's shape — see
  _views/single/contact/default.twig — because it is the same kind of page: a whisper, a
  title, a form, and the ways to get in touch beside it.

  A ROUTE RATHER THAN A SINGLE, and only for now. Everything else here is an element with
  its own address so its copy is written in the control panel, and this page should end up
  the same way. The strings below are placeholders standing in for fields that do not exist
  yet; when the single is made they come from the entry, exactly as contact's do, and this
  file loses its hardcoded words rather than gaining more.

  See craft/config/routes.php for the pattern that reaches it.
#}
{% extends '_layouts/page.twig' %}

{% set tplPath = _self %}

{# The same recolour the contact page uses, since it is the same shape of page. #}
{% set slabModifier = 'b-slab--l600' %}

{% block siteContent %}
    {# CTAs from the globals single — the same source the footer and the contact page use,
       filtered by the visitor's VIP purpose. Somebody who does not want to wait for a
       report should still have a way to reach Jon. #}
    {% set ctas = craft.frontend.ctas() %}

    {% include '_components/content' with {
        whisper: 'Homepage audit',
        title: 'What does your homepage spend its space on?',
        body: '<p>Most homepage advice is a checklist someone wrote about websites in
            general. This is a measurement of yours: we photograph the whole page, not just
            the first screen, cut it where your own markup changes, and work out what share
            of the space goes to each of eight things.</p>
            <p>You get the number, and the annotated screenshot it came from — so if you
            disagree with a section, you can point at it.</p>',
        form: '_components/audit-form',
        ctas: ctas,
        ctasHeading: 'Or just get in touch',
    } only %}
{% endblock %}
